    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: playerController
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 1954674789}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: texts.Array.size
      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: sprites.Array.size
      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'texts.Array.data[0]'
      value: Welcome to Tower Defense, where the aim is to prevent enemies from entering
        your base, represented by the shield symbol. At the top of the screen, you
        can see the number of gold, life points and time until the next wave. You
        lose if your hit points drop to 0.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'texts.Array.data[1]'
      value: "You can start the game by pressing the \u2018Star next wave\u2019 button.
        After that, the waves arrive after a while. However, you can launch the wave
        earlier as soon as the \u2018Star next wave\u2019 button appears. If you
        launch the wave earlier, you'll earn bonus gold according to the time remaining."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'texts.Array.data[2]'
      value: To defend yourself, you need to place towers. The towers have a defined
        position, which you can recognise by the sign.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'texts.Array.data[3]'
      value: Clicking on the panel brings up a menu showing the turrets that can
        be installed and their cost. When you click on a landed turret, you can see
        its stats at the bottom as well as its range. Turrets can also be upgraded,
        increasing their damage, range etc...
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'texts.Array.data[4]'
      value: the turrets will automatically attack enemies within range.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'texts.Array.data[5]'
      value: You can click on the enemies to see their stats.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6174597650260556704, guid: bcbbfee83251f8244be938352bb36305, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'sprites.Array.data[0]'
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 6911672405920476747, guid: fb417b45ebd5aea45af6bb756d98c33a, type: 3}
